-- int-tests-application: headline (a), whole scenarios across groups G1 (the entity), G2 (the charity test), G3 (the principal address), G4 (the decision), G6 (Article 19(5), 19(9)(c), 20(1)(c))
-- and G7 (commencement and the text of the Law).  EXPECTED VALUES were decided by hand from the Law before this module was run (each scenario states its reasoning in a comment):
--   Article 11(4): "If the applicant complies with paragraph (2), with any Regulations under paragraph (3), and with Article 19(5), the Commissioner must register the applicant as a charity if satisfied that" the
--   six matters hold; Article 11(5): "If not so satisfied, the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant"; Article 19(9)(c): the Commissioner "must not ... grant that application until the issue has
--   been determined and any resulting order or notice complied with"; Article 20(1)(c): the court may order "that the entity must not be registered as a charity".

§ `Integration layer -- headline (a): scenarios`

GIVETH A `Readings of the fleet`
fleet MEANS `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`

-- The applicant of most scenarios: a Jersey company with one director who lives in Jersey, advancing education, with a registered office in St Helier.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the Jersey school company` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        standing IS `an applicant for registration`
        purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`))
        facts IS `Int fx a Jersey company` (LIST (`Int fx a natural person resident in Jersey called` "A. Le Brun"))
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun")

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the satisfied application` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the Jersey school company`
        `charity test facts` IS `Int fx the charity test facts with` `Int fx a determination that public benefit is provided`
        application IS `Int fx a complete application lodged on` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        findings IS `Int fx clear findings`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS `Int fx a registered office in Jersey at` "1 Esplanade, St Helier"
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Gorey Schools Limited"
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision to register` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`the decision to refuse` MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` OF `whether to register an applicant, Article 11`, `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `A1: everything in order -- the Commissioner must register the applicant`

-- Education is a head of Article 6(1)(b); the public benefit determination is made; a company established in Jersey is a Jersey entity (Article 2(1)(f), 2(3)(a)), so Article 11(4)(c) is met; the registered office is the principal
-- address (Article 8(4)(a)); the name is not undesirable; the application is complete and Article 19(5) is complied with; no bar on granting. So the Commissioner must register, and the application may be granted.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s `the application may be granted`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s decision EQUALS JUST `the decision to register`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s `the entity has a principal address in Jersey`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s `the name is undesirable`
-- G1 derived the entity: a company, which is a Jersey entity, with the director as governor.
#ASSERT ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s entity)'s `kinds of entity` EQUALS LIST `a company`
#ASSERT ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s entity)'s `is a Jersey entity`
#ASSERT count (((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the satisfied application`)'s entity)'s governors) EQUALS 1

§§ `A2: a governor has reported a matter that is not yet determined -- Article 19(9)(c) bars the grant although the six matters hold`

-- The six matters of Article 11(4) hold, so the duty to register (11(4)) arises; Article 19(9)(c) says the Commissioner must not grant the application until the issue is determined. G4's favoured reading of F4.4: the bar
-- displaces the duty. The Law says "until", so the duty is only postponed: the Commissioner must not YET grant it.
GIVETH A `Person in the case`
`the director who has reported a matter` MEANS
    `Person in the case` WITH
        considered IS (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "A. Le Brun")'s considered
        `facts for the reportable matters` IS `Int fx the clear facts for the reportable matters of` "A. Le Brun"
        `made a report under paragraph (2)` IS TRUE
        `provided a declaration of no reportable matter` IS FALSE
        `reported matter awaiting determination` IS JUST `Int fx a reported matter not yet determined`

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application with an undetermined reported matter` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `Body in the case` WITH
            name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
            standing IS `an applicant for registration`
            purposes IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s purposes
            facts IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s facts
            model IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s model
            people IS LIST `the director who has reported a matter`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS (`the satisfied application`)'s findings
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `opinion on the name`
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with an undetermined reported matter`)'s `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with an undetermined reported matter`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must not yet grant the application`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with an undetermined reported matter`)'s `the application may be granted`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with an undetermined reported matter`)'s decision EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same governor's issue determined and its order complied with: no bar, the Commissioner must register.
GIVETH A `Person in the case`
`the director whose reported matter is settled` MEANS
    `Person in the case` WITH
        considered IS (`the director who has reported a matter`)'s considered
        `facts for the reportable matters` IS (`the director who has reported a matter`)'s `facts for the reportable matters`
        `made a report under paragraph (2)` IS TRUE
        `provided a declaration of no reportable matter` IS FALSE
        `reported matter awaiting determination` IS JUST `Int fx a reported matter determined and complied with`

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application with a settled reported matter` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `Body in the case` WITH
            name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
            standing IS `an applicant for registration`
            purposes IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s purposes
            facts IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s facts
            model IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s model
            people IS LIST `the director whose reported matter is settled`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS (`the satisfied application`)'s findings
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `opinion on the name`
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a settled reported matter`)'s `Article 19(9)(c) bars granting the application`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a settled reported matter`)'s `the application may be granted`
-- F4.4 reading B (the duty to register prevails): the same undetermined matter no longer stops the duty to register; reading C: the two duties conflict and the model refuses.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` (`Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 11 and 12` fleet `reading F4.4 B`) (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with an undetermined reported matter`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must register the applicant`
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` (`Int fx the readings with the reading of Articles 11 and 12` fleet `reading F4.4 C`) (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with an undetermined reported matter`)'s duty

§§ `A3: the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered -- Article 20(1)(c)`

-- A court order under Article 20(1)(c) is a bar on registering. The order is in force on the day asked (Article 20(2)(b)): made 3 March 2026, no time limit, so it is in force on 2 October 2026.
GIVETH AN `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)`
`the order not to register` MEANS
    `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` WITH kind IS `an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity`, `made on` IS YMD 2026 3 3, reach IS `a particular registered charity`, `time limit ends on` IS NOTHING

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application with a court order not to register` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the Jersey school company`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS (`the satisfied application`)'s findings
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `opinion on the name`
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS LIST `the order not to register`
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a court order not to register`)'s `the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a court order not to register`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must not register the applicant`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application with a court order not to register`)'s `the application may be granted`
-- Asked about a day before the order was made (2 March 2026), the court has not yet ordered: the application may be granted.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 3 2) `the application with a court order not to register`)'s `the application may be granted`

§§ `A4: the application is missing the copy of the constitution -- Article 11(2)(b) -- so neither duty arises`

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application without a copy of the constitution` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the Jersey school company`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS `Int fx an application lodged on without a copy of the constitution` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        findings IS (`the satisfied application`)'s findings
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `opinion on the name`
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

-- Article 11(4) needs compliance with paragraph (2); 11(5) is "if not so satisfied", about the six matters (trap T10 case B): an incomplete application raises neither duty on the favoured reading of F4.3.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application without a copy of the constitution`)'s `the application includes what Article 11(2) requires`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application without a copy of the constitution`)'s duty EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application without a copy of the constitution`)'s decision EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application without a copy of the constitution`)'s `the application may be granted`

§§ `A5: a political-party purpose -- Article 6(5) -- fails the charity test, so the Commissioner must refuse`

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the company with a political party purpose` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Gorey Schools Limited"
        standing IS `an applicant for registration`
        purposes IS LIST (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` (`Int fx a charitable purpose` "to advance education in Jersey" `the advancement of education`)), (`Int fx a purpose with clear facts` `Int fx a political party purpose`)
        facts IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s facts
        model IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s model
        people IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s people

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of the company with a political party purpose` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the company with a political party purpose`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS (`the satisfied application`)'s findings
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `opinion on the name`
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

-- Article 6(5): a purpose of advancing a political party is neither a charitable purpose nor ancillary to one; Article 5(1)(a) needs every purpose to be charitable or purely ancillary. So the test fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the company with a political party purpose`)'s `the entity meets the charity test`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the company with a political party purpose`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the company with a political party purpose`)'s decision EQUALS JUST `the decision to refuse`

§§ `A6: a foreign entity with no activity in Jersey -- Article 11(4)(c) -- must be refused`

GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the foreign company` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Normandie Aid SARL"
        standing IS `an applicant for registration`
        purposes IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s purposes
        facts IS `Int fx a foreign body similar to` (LIST `a company`)
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS EMPTY

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of the foreign company` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the foreign company`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS `Int fx findings with no activity in Jersey`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Normandie Aid SARL"
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

-- A body established under the law of another jurisdiction is within Article 2(1)(j) if substantially similar to a body in (a) to (h): here a company (f). It is not a Jersey entity (Article 2(3) names (a) to (h) and
-- the Jersey unincorporated body), and the Commissioner finds no activity in or from Jersey: Article 11(4)(c) fails.
#ASSERT ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the foreign company`)'s entity)'s `kinds of entity` EQUALS LIST `an entity substantially similar to one of the above, established under the law of another jurisdiction`
#ASSERT NOT ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the foreign company`)'s entity)'s `is a Jersey entity`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the foreign company`)'s `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application of the foreign company`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`

