§§ `A8: the application does not state that the declarations are held -- Article 19(5) -- so it is not complete (Article 19(6))`

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application that does not state the declarations` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the Jersey school company`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS (`the satisfied application`)'s findings
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `opinion on the name`
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS FALSE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application that does not state the declarations`)'s `the applicant has complied with Article 19(5)`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) `the application that does not state the declarations`)'s duty EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`

§§ `A13 and A14: an Order under Article 13(9) -- only limb (b) asks for a draft statement of intentions with the application (Article 11(2)(e)(ii)) -- IP29`

-- Article 11(2)(e)(ii) asks for a draft of the proposed statement "if an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to the registered charity".
-- An Order that requires only the details of prescribed payments in the annual return (limb (a)) is not an Order under 13(9)(b), so an application without a draft statement still includes what Article 11(2) requires (A13).
-- An Order that requires a statement of current intentions (limb (b)) does, so the same application is short of Article 11(2) and neither duty arises (A14).
-- (Group G5's composite fact is TRUE for both Orders; wired from it, A13 would come out as incomplete.  See int-tests-red.l4, seam 2.)
GIVETH AN `Order under Article 13(9)`
`an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS TRUE, `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS FALSE, `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE
GIVETH AN `Order under Article 13(9)`
`an Order that requires a statement of intentions` MEANS
    `Order under Article 13(9)` WITH `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)` IS FALSE, `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)` IS TRUE, `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)` IS FALSE
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Int fx the application with Order under Article 13(9) replaced` `the satisfied application` (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`)))'s `the application includes what Article 11(2) requires`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Int fx the application with Order under Article 13(9) replaced` `the satisfied application` (JUST `an Order that requires payment details in the annual return only`)))'s `the application may be granted`
#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Int fx the application with Order under Article 13(9) replaced` `the satisfied application` (JUST `an Order that requires a statement of intentions`)))'s `the application includes what Article 11(2) requires`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2026 10 2) (`Int fx the application with Order under Article 13(9) replaced` `the satisfied application` (JUST `an Order that requires a statement of intentions`)))'s duty EQUALS `no duty to register or to refuse arises because the application does not comply`

§§ `A9 to A12: the day -- commencement (IP4) and the text of the Law (IP2)`

-- 30 April 2018: Part 4 comes into force on 1 May 2018 (R&O.17/2018), so the first Article in the list that is not in force is Article 8.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2018 4 30) `the satisfied application`) BECAUSE "Article 8 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 (Part 4) was not in force on the day asked: it came into force on 1 May 2018"
-- 1 June 2018: the Articles are in force, but no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources, and the kinds of entity depend on the text: group G1 refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2018 6 1) `the satisfied application`) BECAUSE "no text of the Law before 1 January 2019 is among the sources"
-- 27 February 2024: the text changed at 9.30 a.m., but neither text differs on a company applicant: the question is answered.
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2024 2 27) `the satisfied application`)'s `the application may be granted`

-- An NPO body corporate established in Jersey that is none of (c) to (h): within Article 2(1)(ba), which exists only from 16 October 2025. Before it is not an entity at all, so it is not a Jersey entity
-- and (with no activity in Jersey) Article 11(4)(c) fails; from 16 October 2025 it is a Jersey entity by Article 2(3)(a) and the application may be granted.
GIVETH A `Body in the case`
`the NPO body corporate` MEANS
    `Body in the case` WITH
        name IS "Les Amis du Jardin"
        standing IS `an applicant for registration`
        purposes IS (`the Jersey school company`)'s purposes
        facts IS `Int fx an NPO body corporate`
        model IS `Int fx clear model facts`
        people IS LIST (`Int fx a director with nothing to report called` "M. Du Feu")

GIVETH AN `Application in the case`
`the application of the NPO body corporate` MEANS
    `Application in the case` WITH
        body IS `the NPO body corporate`
        `charity test facts` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `charity test facts`
        application IS (`the satisfied application`)'s application
        findings IS `Int fx findings with no activity in Jersey`
        `Order under Article 13(9)` IS NOTHING
        `relief Orders under Article 13(10)` IS EMPTY
        `facts for the principal address` IS (`the satisfied application`)'s `facts for the principal address`
        `opinion on the name` IS `Int fx a name with no objection` "Les Amis du Jardin"
        `the application states that the entity holds declarations` IS TRUE
        `orders of the court` IS EMPTY
        `notices served` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT NOT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2025 10 15) `the application of the NPO body corporate`)'s `the application may be granted`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2025 10 15) `the application of the NPO body corporate`)'s duty EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse to register the applicant`
#ASSERT (`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2025 10 16) `the application of the NPO body corporate`)'s `the application may be granted`
#ASSERT ((`Int (a) may the application be granted` fleet (YMD 2025 10 16) `the application of the NPO body corporate`)'s entity)'s `kinds of entity` EQUALS LIST `a body corporate that is an NPO established under the law of Jersey`
